ain","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:bb590b13d28b16cfe83b2f52ecb4afe53edbbf70bb383b843215b349e64b1917","file":"preprints/Subsphere-methods-for-memory-sample-lower-bounds-in-noiseless-Gaussian-regression-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":53,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ef8a380d4b046d709e5b2dd789d49c9809e9ea2156c25c7fcbc816b93b6194ca","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Subsphere-methods-for-memory-sample-lower-bounds-in-noiseless-Gaussian-regression-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:bb590b13d28b16cfe83b2f52ecb4afe53edbbf70bb383b843215b349e64b1917","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Subsphere-methods-for-memory-sample-lower-bounds-in-noiseless-Gaussian-regression-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L53"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{s:main}\nLet \\(M:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\\) satisfy \\(M(d)=o(d^2)\\).\nThere is a dimension threshold depending only on this memory sequence\nsuch that, for every larger \\(d\\), every \\(0<\\epsilon\\le1/10\\), and\nevery learner in Definition~\\ref{s:model}, the following implication\nholds. If \\(S\\) is uniform on \\(S^{d-1}\\), independently of the\nGaussian rows and learner randomness, and\n\\[\n \\Prob\\{\\arccos\\ip{\\widehat s}{S}\\le\\epsilon\\}\\ge\\frac23,\n\\]\nthen\n\\begin{equation}\\label{s:main-bound}\n T\\ge 2^{-16}d\\log_2(1/\\epsilon).\n\\end{equation}"}
